      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n**Draft until #58795 merges.** Enrolls the three Language Models steps that build mamba-ssm and causal-conv1d from source, and their AMD mirrors, in `automatic_shard` (6 jobs). The source builds take most of a job's setup, and every shard would repeat them; #58795 prebuilds both in the test image, after which sharding these pays for itself. Part of the series that enrolls every remaining test step (#64590-#64599).\n\n## Claims\n\n| Step | Change | AMD mirror |\n|---|---|---|\n| `language-models-test-extended-generation` | enrolled | enrolled |\n| `language-models-tests-granite-l4-compatibility` | enrolled | enrolled |\n| `language-models-tests-hybrid` | fixed 2-way pytest-shard split becomes automatic | same |\n\n## Validation\n\n- `split_check.py`: no step runs the whole suite in each of its jobs.\n- `/ci run` once #58795 has merged and this branch is rebased; until then the mamba builds would repeat per shard.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Hybrid** drops `parallelism: 2` and its `--num-shards/--shard-id` flags (step and mirror), so the planner owns the split.\n- **Timeouts unchanged.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
